WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.967 --> 00:00:02.968
-Today, House Democrats voted

00:00:02.968 --> 00:00:06.238
to admit Washington, D.C.
as the 51st state,

00:00:06.238 --> 00:00:08.540
despite some truly dumb
objections from Republicans,

00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:09.842
who've spent the week

00:00:09.842 --> 00:00:11.911
freaking out about everything
from D.C. statehood

00:00:11.911 --> 00:00:13.679
to voting rights,
to the Green New Deal.

00:00:13.679 --> 00:00:15.782
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:15.782 --> 00:00:19.785
♪♪

00:00:19.785 --> 00:00:21.520
I have to say,
it is such a relief

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:22.655
to not have to care

00:00:22.655 --> 00:00:24.357
about what Donald Trump says
or does anymore.

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:25.691
I mean, he did
a sit-down interview

00:00:25.691 --> 00:00:27.259
with Sean Hannity
earlier this week

00:00:27.259 --> 00:00:30.196
and we haven't mentioned it once
or played a single clip from it.

00:00:30.196 --> 00:00:32.064
If he was still president,
we would've had to cover it,

00:00:32.064 --> 00:00:33.066
but, now,
we can just ignore it.

00:00:33.066 --> 00:00:34.834
It's the same kind
of freedom I felt

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:36.536
once I gave myself permission

00:00:36.536 --> 00:00:39.205
to stop caring about all
the various plotlines

00:00:39.205 --> 00:00:40.573
in the
Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:00:40.573 --> 00:00:42.942
It used to be that, when I
watched one of those movies,

00:00:42.942 --> 00:00:46.279
I was trying to retrace
every decision Dr. Strange made

00:00:46.279 --> 00:00:48.581
in the time loop
that, somehow, led to the blip

00:00:48.581 --> 00:00:50.116
and The Avengers
defeating Thanos.

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:51.917
And then, you know what?
I gave myself permission

00:00:51.917 --> 00:00:53.552
to just sit back, relax,

00:00:53.552 --> 00:00:55.421
and enjoy Loki's antics.

00:00:55.421 --> 00:00:57.056
Oh, you trickster, you!

00:00:57.056 --> 00:00:59.058
I cannot wait to see
what kind of goofs

00:00:59.058 --> 00:01:00.593
you get up to with Owen Wilson.

00:01:00.593 --> 00:01:02.428
Although, as much as I love
Tom Hiddleston,

00:01:02.428 --> 00:01:05.799
I really wish mid-2000s
Vince Vaughn was playing Loki.

00:01:05.799 --> 00:01:07.499
[ As Wilson ]
I'm just not sure
I can trust you, Loki.

00:01:07.499 --> 00:01:09.935
[ As Vaughn ]
Buddy, buddy, buddy,
you're breaking my heart, here.

00:01:09.935 --> 00:01:11.437
I would never lie to you.

00:01:11.437 --> 00:01:13.072
Sure, I would embellish
for effect, sure.

00:01:13.072 --> 00:01:14.240
Have I told a fib,
here and there?

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:15.641
Guilty as charged.
And, if that's a crime,

00:01:15.641 --> 00:01:17.343
by all means, lock me up
and throw away the key.

00:01:17.343 --> 00:01:19.846
But to lie to you?
No, not ever. Not ever, buddy.

00:01:19.846 --> 00:01:21.513
[ As Wilson ]
Alright, I'll give you
the Tesseract, Loki,

00:01:21.513 --> 00:01:22.682
but I'm vouching for you, here.

00:01:22.682 --> 00:01:23.783
Bring it back.

00:01:23.783 --> 00:01:25.351
[ Laughter ]
Even when I scroll Twitter

00:01:25.351 --> 00:01:27.153
and see stills
from that interview,

00:01:27.153 --> 00:01:29.155
it's a little shocking
to remember that he even exists

00:01:29.155 --> 00:01:30.790
and that he still
looks like this.

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:33.426
I mean, presidents are supposed
to look more relaxed,

00:01:33.426 --> 00:01:34.560
once they're out of office.

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:36.195
Trump looks like he's been
up all night,

00:01:36.195 --> 00:01:38.297
trying to find the sailboat
in a Magic Eye poster.

00:01:38.297 --> 00:01:40.933
Meanwhile, Obama somehow
looks ten years younger.

00:01:40.933 --> 00:01:43.169
He's cruising around
with his shirt unbuttoned,

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:45.371
like the CEO
of a music festival

00:01:45.371 --> 00:01:47.873
and he's doing a podcast
at Bruce Springsteen.

00:01:47.873 --> 00:01:49.542
Soon, he's going to start
taking over

00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:51.477
the Little Steven parts
in "Glory Days."

00:01:51.477 --> 00:01:52.645
[ As Obama ]
♪ Oh ♪

00:01:52.645 --> 00:01:53.846
♪ Alright! ♪

00:01:53.846 --> 00:01:55.214
♪ Oh ♪

00:01:55.214 --> 00:01:56.382
♪ Oh, yeah ♪

00:01:56.382 --> 00:01:58.117
[ Laughter ]
I guess that's the difference

00:01:58.117 --> 00:02:00.687
between being a former
president who's beloved

00:02:00.687 --> 00:02:02.855
and a former president who's
under criminal investigation,

00:02:02.855 --> 00:02:04.223
although, I will say,

00:02:04.223 --> 00:02:06.325
before Trump even answered
a single question --

00:02:06.325 --> 00:02:08.227
and I know, I said
we're going to ignore it,

00:02:08.227 --> 00:02:10.096
but I'm like
a moth to a flame, baby!

00:02:10.096 --> 00:02:11.431
Plus, it's what
the audience wants.

00:02:11.431 --> 00:02:14.466
Right, you guys?

00:02:14.466 --> 00:02:16.169
[ Laughter ]
Thanks for having my back, Baze.

00:02:16.169 --> 00:02:17.670
Where was I?

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:19.906
Oh, yeah, before Trump
answered a single question,

00:02:19.906 --> 00:02:23.309
the interview was already off
to an absolutely ludicrous start

00:02:23.309 --> 00:02:24.677
when Hannity said this.

00:02:24.677 --> 00:02:27.179
-Alright, so,
I know a lot of people

00:02:27.179 --> 00:02:28.781 line:0%
that are around you every day.

00:02:28.781 --> 00:02:30.649 line:0%
This is what
they're all telling me.

00:02:30.649 --> 00:02:32.384 line:0%
You are working
as hard as you did

00:02:32.384 --> 00:02:34.120 line:0%
when you were
in the White House,

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:36.989 line:0%
except,
you play a little golf more.

00:02:36.989 --> 00:02:40.793 line:0%
That you're keeping
an insane schedule

00:02:40.793 --> 00:02:42.427 line:0%
seven days a week.

00:02:42.427 --> 00:02:44.363 line:0%
You really don't stop.

00:02:44.363 --> 00:02:46.732
-Man, there are softballs
and then, there are tee balls,

00:02:46.732 --> 00:02:48.401
but that was like
Hannity put the ball

00:02:48.401 --> 00:02:50.470
on the other side of the fence
and then told Trump

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:52.638
to walk around the bases
like he hit a dinger.

00:02:52.638 --> 00:02:54.340
[ As Hannity ]
You did it, sir, not me.

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:56.242
Now, let's see
that home run trot.

00:02:56.242 --> 00:02:57.410
What was the next question?

00:02:57.410 --> 00:02:58.644
[ As Hannity ]
I heard there were a lot of

00:02:58.644 --> 00:03:00.746
behind-the-scenes pranks
at the White House.

00:03:00.746 --> 00:03:03.316
[ As Trump ]
Oh, yeah. One time, we tied
a chicken nugget to a Roomba

00:03:03.316 --> 00:03:05.184
and made Eric chase it
for three days.

00:03:05.184 --> 00:03:06.185
It wasn't all laughs, though.

00:03:06.185 --> 00:03:07.520
He came back.

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:09.221
[ Laughter ]
But, as that clip proves,

00:03:09.221 --> 00:03:11.057
as much as a relief it is

00:03:11.057 --> 00:03:13.392
to not have to cover
or care about Trump anymore,

00:03:13.392 --> 00:03:14.894
the Republican Party
he left behind

00:03:14.894 --> 00:03:18.130
is still very much committed
to both the ideology

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:19.666
and the performance
of Trumpism --

00:03:19.666 --> 00:03:22.268
the paranoia,
conspiracy theories, racism,

00:03:22.268 --> 00:03:24.036
and lies about everything
from coronavirus

00:03:24.036 --> 00:03:27.139
to climate change, to voting
reforms, to D.C. statehood.

00:03:27.139 --> 00:03:28.474
In fact, in some cases,

00:03:28.474 --> 00:03:31.311
they're still pushing some
of Trump's trademark lies,

00:03:31.311 --> 00:03:33.445
ones you may have
even forgotten about,

00:03:33.445 --> 00:03:35.347
like his debunked
and dangerous claim

00:03:35.347 --> 00:03:38.017
that hydroxychloroquine
can cure coronavirus.

00:03:38.017 --> 00:03:40.219
Remember that oldie
from summer 2020?

00:03:40.219 --> 00:03:41.487
Well, it's back,
thanks to former

00:03:41.487 --> 00:03:44.023
Housing Secretary Ben Carson,
who resurrected

00:03:44.023 --> 00:03:46.459
the hydroxychloroquine lie
on Fox News this week

00:03:46.459 --> 00:03:49.729
and even Fox had a hard time
letting him get away with it.

00:03:49.729 --> 00:03:52.364 line:0%
-We as a nation, for instance,

00:03:52.364 --> 00:03:56.603 line:0%
wanted to be focused only
on one thing -- vaccinations.

00:03:56.603 --> 00:03:59.339 line:0%
There were people telling us,
you know,

00:03:59.339 --> 00:04:04.610 line:0%
there are ivermectin and other
kinds of things that work --

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:06.545 line:0%
hydroxychloroquine
-There's a number

00:04:06.545 --> 00:04:07.814 line:0%
-has worked as well.
-of medical experts who've

00:04:07.814 --> 00:04:09.515 line:0%
looked at that, Doctor,
as you know,

00:04:09.515 --> 00:04:12.918 line:0%
and pooh-poohed that connection
with hydroxychloroquine.

00:04:12.918 --> 00:04:14.820 line:0%
-You know, you just said,
you know, a bunch of people

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:16.789 line:0%
have pooh-poohed
the hydrochloroquine,

00:04:16.789 --> 00:04:18.858 line:0%
but the evidence is there.

00:04:18.858 --> 00:04:20.092
-It's nice to have a marker

00:04:20.092 --> 00:04:22.995
that shows exactly
when Ben Carson fell asleep.

00:04:22.995 --> 00:04:24.496
It's like when your girlfriend
falls asleep

00:04:24.496 --> 00:04:27.433
during "Law &amp; Order" and says,
"Hey, was it the husband?"

00:04:27.433 --> 00:04:28.901
No, they ruled the husband out
five minutes in.

00:04:28.901 --> 00:04:30.302
And also, God forgive me,

00:04:30.302 --> 00:04:33.339
I really don't want this
to be my primary focus,

00:04:33.339 --> 00:04:36.809
but I do love that Cavuto
inadvertently got Carson

00:04:36.809 --> 00:04:38.210
to repeat the word pooh-pooh.

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:41.881
You never want to hear a doctor
use the word pooh-pooh,

00:04:41.881 --> 00:04:45.318
unless they're
a gastroenterologist.

00:04:45.318 --> 00:04:46.519
[ Laughter ]

00:04:46.519 --> 00:04:49.355
Where's the rimshot?
Is Fred not here today?

00:04:49.355 --> 00:04:52.992
Because we needed
the rimshot there.

00:04:52.992 --> 00:04:54.660
Okay, but can we just get him
to record a rimshot,

00:04:54.660 --> 00:04:56.428
so we have something to play?

00:04:56.428 --> 00:05:00.033
Do we have anything on hand
for the end of that joke?

00:05:00.033 --> 00:05:01.800
Okay.

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:03.435
Alright, I'll do it again.

00:05:03.435 --> 00:05:05.938
You never want to hear a doctor
use the word pooh-pooh,

00:05:05.938 --> 00:05:07.973
unless they're
a gastroenterologist.

00:05:07.973 --> 00:05:10.709
-♪ Shots, shots, shots, shots,
shot-shots ♪

00:05:10.709 --> 00:05:12.511
[ Laughter ]
Why that?

00:05:12.511 --> 00:05:14.780
Oh, right, right, right,
because we already used

00:05:14.780 --> 00:05:17.182
our entire music allowance
when we played it on Monday?

00:05:17.182 --> 00:05:19.652
[ Laughter ]
Fine, but that's the last time
I want to hear it!

00:05:19.652 --> 00:05:20.953
Also, can we go back to this?

00:05:20.953 --> 00:05:22.588 line:0%
-The evidence is there.

00:05:22.588 --> 00:05:23.789 line:0%
-No, it's not.
Where are you getting

00:05:23.789 --> 00:05:25.191 line:0%
this evidence from?
Who are you talking to?

00:05:25.191 --> 00:05:26.258 line:0%
[ As Lindell ]
It cures everything --

00:05:26.258 --> 00:05:28.127 line:0%
coronavirus, hemorrhoids,

00:05:28.127 --> 00:05:30.028
joint pain, sleep deprivation.

00:05:30.028 --> 00:05:34.099
It even acts as a steroid
to help you build muscle mass

00:05:34.099 --> 00:05:36.702
so you can fight antifa
when they come to your door.

00:05:36.702 --> 00:05:38.637
You give 'em a little one-two.

00:05:38.637 --> 00:05:40.640
[ Laughter ]
Or you can become an athlete

00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:43.042
and win the Super Bowl
with Da Bears!

00:05:43.042 --> 00:05:44.510
[ Laughter ]

00:05:44.510 --> 00:05:47.013
You know, usually we film
"Late Night" in New York,

00:05:47.013 --> 00:05:49.182
but on Thursdays, we do it
from Callback City, baby!

00:05:49.182 --> 00:05:50.449
[ Laughter ]

00:05:50.449 --> 00:05:52.985
We get five cents back
for every joke we recycle.

00:05:52.985 --> 00:05:54.420
Happy Earth Day.

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:55.721
[ Laughter ]
Anyway, the point is

00:05:55.721 --> 00:05:58.257
the GOP is still very much
committed to the toxic,

00:05:58.257 --> 00:06:01.193
paranoid, authoritarian
ideology of Trumpism.

00:06:01.193 --> 00:06:03.395
People like Matt Gaetz
and Marjorie Taylor Greene

00:06:03.395 --> 00:06:04.530
are perfect examples.

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:05.831
As President Biden prepared

00:06:05.831 --> 00:06:07.934
to hold a climate summit
with world leaders

00:06:07.934 --> 00:06:11.037
and as progressives,
led by Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez,

00:06:11.037 --> 00:06:12.804
reintroduced
the Green New Deal,

00:06:12.804 --> 00:06:14.740
Marjorie Taylor Greene,
who craves attention,

00:06:14.740 --> 00:06:16.842
challenged AOC
to a debate on Twitter,

00:06:16.842 --> 00:06:19.578
which, for AOC, is not
even worth responding to.

00:06:19.578 --> 00:06:22.781
It's like George Foreman getting
challenged to a boxing match

00:06:22.781 --> 00:06:23.782
by DJ Qualls.

00:06:23.782 --> 00:06:24.883
Quallback.

00:06:24.883 --> 00:06:26.152
[ Laughter ]
But Greene persisted,

00:06:26.152 --> 00:06:28.187
posting a photo of herself
yesterday,

00:06:28.187 --> 00:06:31.224
talking to AOC on the House
floor, in a tweet that said...

00:06:39.765 --> 00:06:41.267
First of all,
I doubt AOC agreed.

00:06:41.267 --> 00:06:42.602
Second, you want us
to be impressed

00:06:42.602 --> 00:06:43.836
that you can read 14 pages?

00:06:43.836 --> 00:06:45.371
My cable bill
is longer than that.

00:06:45.371 --> 00:06:46.906
The script for this segment

00:06:46.906 --> 00:06:49.008
is usually like
three times as long,

00:06:49.008 --> 00:06:50.275
much to Shoemaker's chagrin.

00:06:50.275 --> 00:06:52.044
That's right, his chagrin.

00:06:52.044 --> 00:06:53.713
You see, as a producer,
it's Shoemaker's job

00:06:53.713 --> 00:06:55.847
to make sure the entire show
fits into an hour

00:06:55.847 --> 00:06:57.650
and that it starts on time
and, you know, works

00:06:57.650 --> 00:06:58.884
as a coherent television show.

00:06:58.884 --> 00:07:00.385
And, every day,
we do a hilarious prank

00:07:00.385 --> 00:07:02.454
where we tell him "Closer Look"
will be a normal length

00:07:02.454 --> 00:07:04.857
and then, when Sal turns it in,
it's got nine different tangents

00:07:04.857 --> 00:07:06.324
about TV shows from the '80s

00:07:06.324 --> 00:07:08.694
and it's longer than the final
episode of "M-A-S-H."

00:07:08.694 --> 00:07:09.795
Suicide may be painless,

00:07:09.795 --> 00:07:12.532
but cutting his jokes
hurt Sal deeply.

00:07:12.532 --> 00:07:14.233
You see, "Suicide Is Painless"
is the name

00:07:14.233 --> 00:07:16.501
of the "M-A-S-H" song,
which doesn't have lyrics,

00:07:16.501 --> 00:07:18.804
but it does have lyrics
in the original "M-A-S-H" movie,

00:07:18.804 --> 00:07:20.372
which is from 1970,

00:07:20.372 --> 00:07:22.040
which is also
where Shoemaker's from.

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:25.644
[ Laughter ]
Oh! And he's looking
chagrined again.

00:07:25.644 --> 00:07:28.080
Anyway, Greene helpfully
followed up this morning

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:29.782
with another tweet,
where she informed us

00:07:29.782 --> 00:07:31.651
that she had, in fact,
read the bill

00:07:31.651 --> 00:07:33.753
and was now ready
for the debate, tweeting...

00:07:38.224 --> 00:07:39.892
Okay.
Thanks for keeping us posted.

00:07:39.892 --> 00:07:43.128
Greene's just dying to grab
some of AOC's spotlight.

00:07:43.128 --> 00:07:45.764
She reminds me of the doorman
at my old building,

00:07:45.764 --> 00:07:47.433
who always said, "You should
have me on your show.

00:07:47.433 --> 00:07:48.967
A lot of crazy stories
happen here.

00:07:48.967 --> 00:07:50.403
One time, a package game,

00:07:50.403 --> 00:07:52.705
but it was
for a different address."

00:07:52.705 --> 00:07:54.373
[ Laughter ]

00:07:54.373 --> 00:07:56.275
But Greene's a perfect avatar
of Trumpism

00:07:56.275 --> 00:07:57.576
because it's all performance.

00:07:57.576 --> 00:07:59.678
I mean, she admitted
she hadn't even read the bill

00:07:59.678 --> 00:08:01.580
before she challenged AOC
to a debate.

00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:02.981
That's the state
of the modern GOP.

00:08:02.981 --> 00:08:05.183
We saw it on display
yet again this week

00:08:05.183 --> 00:08:06.518
during hearings
on voting rights.

00:08:06.518 --> 00:08:08.787
For example, former Georgia
gubernatorial candidate

00:08:08.787 --> 00:08:11.323
Stacey Abrams testified
in the Senate

00:08:11.323 --> 00:08:14.059
about Georgia's Draconian
new voter suppression laws.

00:08:14.059 --> 00:08:16.729
Louisiana Senator John Kennedy
challenged Abrams

00:08:16.729 --> 00:08:18.597
to list off her objections
to the bill

00:08:18.597 --> 00:08:20.766
and you could tell
he was not ready

00:08:20.766 --> 00:08:24.003
for her to actually have such
a detailed, substantive list.

00:08:24.003 --> 00:08:28.373
-Tell me, specifically,
just give me a list,

00:08:28.373 --> 00:08:31.943
of the provisions
that you object to.

00:08:31.943 --> 00:08:34.746
-I object to the provisions
that remove access

00:08:34.746 --> 00:08:36.014
to the right to vote,

00:08:36.014 --> 00:08:37.583
that shorten the federal
runoff period

00:08:37.583 --> 00:08:39.385
from nine weeks to four weeks...
-Okay.

00:08:39.385 --> 00:08:41.387
-...restrict the time
that a voter can request

00:08:41.387 --> 00:08:43.622
and return an absentee ballot
application.

00:08:43.622 --> 00:08:45.858
-Right.
-It requires that a voter have

00:08:45.858 --> 00:08:49.361
a photo identification or some
other form of identification

00:08:49.361 --> 00:08:50.962
that they're willing
to surrender,

00:08:50.962 --> 00:08:54.800
in order to participate
in absentee ballot process.

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:56.401
-What else?

00:08:56.401 --> 00:09:00.072
-It eliminates over 300 hours
of dropbox availability.

00:09:00.072 --> 00:09:01.774
-Okay. What else?

00:09:01.774 --> 00:09:05.110
-It bans nearly all
out-of-precinct votes.

00:09:05.110 --> 00:09:07.546
-Is that everything?

00:09:07.546 --> 00:09:09.282
-No, it is not. [ Laughs ]
No, sir.

00:09:09.282 --> 00:09:12.250
It restricts
the hours of operation.

00:09:12.250 --> 00:09:14.320
Instead of those hours being
from 7:00 to 7:00,

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:15.954
they're now from 9:00 to 5:00,

00:09:15.954 --> 00:09:17.723
which may have
an effect on voters

00:09:17.723 --> 00:09:22.127
who cannot vote during business
hours during early voting.

