00:11:27.319 --> 00:11:29.555
These guys talk about the
so-called socialist utopia

00:11:29.555 --> 00:11:31.890 line:0%
as if it was a bad thing,
when polls repeatedly show

00:11:31.890 --> 00:11:33.558 line:0%
that the core ideas
of what progressives

00:11:33.558 --> 00:11:34.860 line:0%
are actually proposing

00:11:34.860 --> 00:11:36.996 line:0%
are overwhelmingly popular
with voters.

00:11:36.996 --> 00:11:38.530 line:0%
In fact, that's why
they're opposed

00:11:38.530 --> 00:11:41.200 line:0%
to rebalancing our democracy --
because, if we do,

00:11:41.200 --> 00:11:43.502 line:0%
those popular ideas have a much
better chance of becoming a law.

00:11:43.502 --> 00:11:45.170 line:0%
Republicans are like
substitute teachers

00:11:45.170 --> 00:11:47.840
who threaten to punish their
class by putting on a movie,

00:11:47.840 --> 00:11:49.608
instead of continuing
with the lesson plan.

00:11:49.608 --> 00:11:52.110
"Look, if you guys don't want
to learn fractals,

00:11:52.110 --> 00:11:53.545
then I'll have no choice

00:11:53.545 --> 00:11:56.181
but to make you watch 'Amadeus'
on laser disc

00:11:56.181 --> 00:11:57.516
